From c21701dbd0cb17326970e10a25029f1abb7811e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asuvath MS <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:21:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] PCI: imx6: power the i.MX6Q PHY up again on core reset
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ADLINK specific]
 deassert

imx_pcie_host_init() enables the clocks before it asserts the core
reset; mainline v6.18 does it the other way round. For IMX6Q, enabling
the clocks powers the PHY up (imx6q_pcie_enable_ref_clk() clears
IMX6Q_GPR1_PCIE_TEST_PD), but imx6q_pcie_core_reset() sets TEST_PD again
on assert and does nothing on deassert. The PHY stays powered down, and
the DBI accesses that follow host_init hang the bus.

On an i.MX6 Solo (ADLINK LEC-iMX6) the board froze about 0.25 s after
"imx6q-pcie 1ffc000.pcie: host bridge /soc/pcie@1ffc000 ranges:", with
no further output. Booting with initcall_blacklist=imx_pcie_init avoided
the freeze.

Power the PHY up again when the core reset is deasserted.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pci-imx6.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pci-imx6.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pci-imx6.c
index 5a7b96a526a8..0f7fb9d95b37 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pci-imx6.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pci-imx6.c
@@ -884,8 +884,14 @@ static int imx6qp_pcie_core_reset(struct imx_pcie *imx_pcie, bool assert)
 
 static int imx6q_pcie_core_reset(struct imx_pcie *imx_pcie, bool assert)
 {
+	/*
+	 * imx_pcie_host_init() enables the clocks, which powers the PHY up,
+	 * before it asserts the core reset, which powers the PHY down again.
+	 * Power it up on deassert, or the DBI accesses that follow hang the
+	 * bus.
+	 */
 	if (!assert)
-		return 0;
+		return imx6q_pcie_enable_ref_clk(imx_pcie, true);
 
 	regmap_set_bits(imx_pcie->iomuxc_gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1, IMX6Q_GPR1_PCIE_TEST_PD);
 	regmap_set_bits(imx_pcie->iomuxc_gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1, IMX6Q_GPR1_PCIE_REF_CLK_EN);
